Original content in README.md and docs/assets/evaluation-purpose.svg is also
licensed under MIT.

The MIT grant covers these original files individually. A combined work that
incorporates AGPL-covered HarnessMinimizer code must comply with the AGPL unless
covered by a separate commercial agreement. The MIT notices do not relicense
the HarnessMinimizer code or third-party components used by these files.

The statements describing this repository as an evaluation artifact identify
its intended purpose. They do not impose an additional research-only condition
on permissions granted by the applicable licenses.

3. Third-party components and benchmark materials
-----------------------------------------------

Upstream copyright notices, permissions, and license conditions remain
applicable to third-party material under either HarnessMinimizer licensing
option. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES and THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/ for component details.

LLVM material retains Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception terms. Upstream treereduce
material retains its MIT terms. Separately obtained Perses engines retain
their GPL-3.0-or-later terms. The HarnessMinimizer installers and modifications
retain the terms identified in their own notices.

The MIT grant for evaluation code does not cover benchmark harnesses, crash
inputs, target libraries, or other upstream materials in benchmark/. Their
applicable permissions and notices remain in effect. Other tools and packages
downloaded by the Dockerfile or installers retain their own license terms.
